---
// The old Wix editor shop's product address (/product-page/<slug>): search results, old emails
// and social posts still link to it. Products kept their slugs, so send them to /products/<slug>,
// which shows its own "not found" page for a product that has since gone. The slug is passed on
// exactly as it came (still URL-encoded), so nothing is decoded and encoded twice.
const slug = Astro.url.pathname.slice("/product-page/".length);
return Astro.redirect(`/products/${slug}`, 301);
---
